Sysop Note 3.0 - Copyrite Bulldog Productions March 1997
--------------------------------------------------------

Introduction
------------

First Of All Thanx For Having A Look At This Program, This Is The Third
Version Of Sysop Note, And Will Probably Not The Last.. Previous
Versions Of Sysop Note Have Needed Keyfiles, I Have Decided To Make This
One Keyfile Free! This Is Mainly Because I Am Currently Working On A
Massive Cnet RPG Game And I Can't Be Bothered To Have Keyfiles On Programs
As Small As This One! :)) 

Installation
------------

If You Have The Older Versions Of Sysop Note Just Delete Them As You Will
Not Need Them At All Anymore.. Now Obviously You Have Unpacked This
(Otherwise How Would You Be Reading This Document <G>) Now You Should Have
The Following Files In A Drawer Called SYSOPNOTE3

SYSOPNOTE3 -+
            +-- details.data (Saved Details Do Not Edit)
            +-- Editor.rexx (Editor Program Do Not Edit)
            +-- Sysopnote3.rexx (Main Program Do No Edit)
            +-- wait.rexx (Small "Press A Key" Program)
            +-- Sysopnote3.Doc ( This Document File)
            +-- Screen_Shots -+
            |                 +- editor.iff (Iff Picture Of The Editor)
            |                 +- mainscreen.iff (Iff Pic Of The Mainscreen)
            +-- Messages -+
                          +- 1 (The First Message Do Not Edit)

If You Are Missing Any Of Theses Files Call Bad Obsession And Get The
One(s) You Need! :))

Ok Move The Drawer SYSOPNOTE3 into PFILES: Now Load Up systext:sys.welcome
In Your Favourite Text Editor (CED Is The Best) now At The Bottom Of That
Text File (Or Where Ever You Want) Put The Following Line :

{#0pfiles:sysopnote3/sysopnote3.rexx}

^
+------- Remember This Is A CTRL+Q :))

Thats It!! :)) Now When You Log On It'll Display A Random News Bulletin Or
Note! Now To Edit The Notes! :) This Is The Fun Bit!

When The Sysop (You) Logs On To The BBS At First You Will Get My BBS Advert
As The News Bulletin, And At The Bottom You Will BE Asked If You Want To
Enter The Editor Program, Say "YES" Here! You Will Have Now Enter The
Program.. You Have Several Options All Of Which Are Easy To Use, The Lowest
And Highest Access Boxes Are For Entering The Editor... You May Have A
Co-sysop you want to use the Program.. So For Example If You Want Your
Co-sysops To Be Able To Use The Editor And Their Access Level Is 30 You
Would Have 30 in the Lowest Access And 31 In The Highest! Simple..
Number Of Bulletins Is How Many Bulletins You Have Entered.. Now For Titles
You Enter The Title Of The Message, Then Move Over And Enter The Message
Using CNets In Built Editor.. Do This For As Many Messages As You Want/Need
And Thats It.. Remember To Save Or You Will Lose It All! :) <G>

